00:22:20.464 --> 00:22:24.301
[Chen] <i>Regarding the murthehelp system.</i>
<i>I will leave it to your discretion</i>

250
00:22:24.385 --> 00:22:27.137
<i>on how to take over and move forward</i>
<i>with the business.</i>

251
00:22:28.055 --> 00:22:32.893
{\an8}<i>If you are successful. I will entrust</i>
<i>the entirety of Babylon Korea to you.</i>

252
00:22:33.894 --> 00:22:36.313
[â™ª tense music playing]

253
00:22:41.151 --> 00:22:44.029
[Minhye] She's staying in a hotel
that's not very far from Babylon.

254
00:22:45.573 --> 00:22:49.285
[Jinwoo] Since it's just a regular hotel.
it should be fairly easy to gain access.

255
00:22:52.663 --> 00:22:55.082
[Minhye] I guarantee
it won't be as easy as you think.

256
00:22:55.165 --> 00:22:57.501
[guide. in Chinese]
We will have breakfast together.

257
00:22:57.585 --> 00:23:01.839
And depart at eight o'clock sharp tomorrow
to begin our sightseeing schedule.

258
00:23:01.922 --> 00:23:05.259
Depart at eight o'clock. Understood!

259
00:23:05.342 --> 00:23:11.098
That's all for today's schedule
and you can rest in your rooms.

260
00:23:11.807 --> 00:23:13.058
[camera shutters click rapidly]

261
00:23:13.267 --> 00:23:17.396
[guide] The convenience store is
on the first floor

262
00:23:17.479 --> 00:23:19.690
and you can use it freely. anytime.

263
00:23:27.489 --> 00:23:28.490
[elevator chimes]

264
00:23:38.584 --> 00:23:39.627
[in English] Why are you up here?

265
00:23:39.710 --> 00:23:42.880
[in Chinese] Huh? Where's everybody?

266
00:23:42.963 --> 00:23:45.174
Strange. Did I get off on the wrong floor?

267
00:23:45.257 --> 00:23:48.052
[in English] This floor is fully booked
for conference participants only.

268
00:23:49.803 --> 00:23:50.804
[Minhye. in Chinese] Really?

269
00:23:50.888 --> 00:23:51.889
[bodyguard. in English] I'm sorry?

270
00:23:52.473 --> 00:23:54.475
[in Chinese] It's nothing. Nothing.
I didn't understand.

271
00:23:54.558 --> 00:23:58.103
Oh. it's okay.
Wow. but you're really tall. aren't you?

272
00:23:59.104 --> 00:24:00.272
[in English] What's going on?

273
00:24:00.356 --> 00:24:02.399
A Chinese tourist came up here by mistake.

274
00:24:09.657 --> 00:24:11.241
[Minhye] It looks like that woman
and her little sidekick

275
00:24:11.325 --> 00:24:12.910
are staying on the same floor.

276
00:24:13.994 --> 00:24:15.663
Should I eliminate them when I can?

277
00:24:16.997 --> 00:24:18.666
I can probably do it pretty easily.

278
00:24:20.709 --> 00:24:21.752
No. thanks.

279
00:24:22.962 --> 00:24:26.924
Even if you eliminate them. Babylon will
just keep sending their replacements.

280
00:24:27.007 --> 00:24:28.801
Do you know her?

281
00:24:29.843 --> 00:24:32.096
When I was in the special forces.

282
00:24:32.179 --> 00:24:34.932
we had an operation to rescue hostages
in Southeast Asia.

283
00:24:35.015 --> 00:24:36.850
That's the only time we've met.

284
00:24:37.601 --> 00:24:40.562
There were Koreans
amongst the Japanese hostages.

285
00:24:40.646 --> 00:24:43.607
Since Japan couldn't deploy troops.
Babylon was called in.

286
00:24:44.650 --> 00:24:46.902
You said. in Hanam-do.
the Babylon team leader was

287
00:24:46.986 --> 00:24:48.070
a Japanese woman. right?

288
00:24:52.116 --> 00:24:55.411
If memory serves correct.
her code name is Q.

289
00:24:56.495 --> 00:24:57.997
[â™ª soft pensive music playing]

290
00:24:58.080 --> 00:24:59.415
[sighs]

291
00:24:59.915 --> 00:25:03.043
Cheolseung.
look into the team leader and Q.

292
00:25:03.127 --> 00:25:05.838
and include all of their team members
that entered Korea.

293
00:25:05.921 --> 00:25:07.840
Get all the detailed information you can.

294
00:25:08.674 --> 00:25:09.883
[Q] <i>I'm Q.</i>

295
00:25:09.967 --> 00:25:12.511
The next time we meet.
we'll go have a drink together.

296
00:25:12.594 --> 00:25:14.013
[in Japanese] Thank you.

297
00:25:14.096 --> 00:25:16.432
[in English]
Long time no see. Jeong Jinman.

298
00:25:17.016 --> 00:25:18.392
[phone buzzing]

299
00:25:28.610 --> 00:25:29.653
ATTORNEY JANG INSEOP

300
00:25:29.737 --> 00:25:32.156
[Cheolseung]
"Negotiation requested." [scoffs]

301
00:25:32.281 --> 00:25:35.617
Those dumb assholes always have
to fuck around and find out the hard way.

302
00:25:35.701 --> 00:25:37.202
[Jinwoo] We can't do this now.

303
00:25:37.286 --> 00:25:39.038
We don't have enough manpower.

304
00:25:39.121 --> 00:25:41.165
Code Yellow took heavy losses
on Hanam-do Island.

305
00:25:41.248 --> 00:25:42.958
Our Code Reds are scattered.

306
00:25:43.042 --> 00:25:45.169
They're waiting to see what happens.

307
00:25:46.795 --> 00:25:50.049
Right. it could be dangerous.
It's not time to negotiate.

308
00:25:50.132 --> 00:25:53.052
Let's secure a safe house first.
And then we can move Jian.

309
00:25:53.135 --> 00:25:54.762
[Jian] Am I some kind of object?

310
00:25:55.637 --> 00:25:57.431
Move me wherever you want?

311
00:25:59.183 --> 00:26:00.851
Over and over.

312
00:26:00.934 --> 00:26:02.478
Without ever negotiating.

313
00:26:05.022 --> 00:26:06.982
You hide. then fight and move.

314
00:26:07.066 --> 00:26:09.902
You repeat the cycle again and again.
And then what?

315
00:26:10.486 --> 00:26:12.738
How many people are gonna die
to protect me?

316
00:26:14.114 --> 00:26:18.202
Do you even know
how many people on Hanam-do Island died?

317
00:26:19.870 --> 00:26:20.913
[scoffs]

318
00:26:22.289 --> 00:26:25.918
When Uncle Jinwoo dies
and Minhye <i>Eonni</i> dies. does this end?

319
00:26:27.252 --> 00:26:28.712
I won't accept that.

320
00:26:28.796 --> 00:26:31.423
I'm not allowing any of you
to sacrifice yourselves.

321
00:26:33.133 --> 00:26:34.218
Do you understand?

322
00:26:38.097 --> 00:26:39.515
That's why I came back.

323
00:26:50.359 --> 00:26:53.904
All right. What's your plan. then?

324
00:26:54.655 --> 00:26:57.199
What are you going to do
to prevent all of usâ€¦

325
00:26:57.991 --> 00:26:59.243
from being sacrificed?

326
00:27:00.744 --> 00:27:01.995
Whatever I can.

327
00:27:02.079 --> 00:27:03.413
[scoffs]

328
00:27:07.292 --> 00:27:08.544
Listen up. Jeong Jian.

329
00:27:10.254 --> 00:27:12.756
It's not possible to negotiate
without strength.

330
00:27:13.632 --> 00:27:15.425
You can't just talk a big game.

331
00:27:15.509 --> 00:27:18.345
You better put your money
where your mouth is first.

332
00:27:18.428 --> 00:27:19.638
You need to prove it.

333
00:27:21.140 --> 00:27:22.224
Hm.

334
00:27:22.683 --> 00:27:23.725
I get it.

335
00:27:25.477 --> 00:27:26.603
I'll prove it to you.

336
00:27:28.438 --> 00:27:29.940
Tell me what to do. I'll do it.

337
00:27:30.732 --> 00:27:33.735
[rain pouring]

338
00:27:35.404 --> 00:27:37.656
[â™ª tense music playing]

339
00:27:45.873 --> 00:27:48.667
[voicemail] <i>The customer you have dialed</i>
<i>cannot answer your call.</i>

340
00:27:48.750 --> 00:27:50.711
<i>Please hang up and try the call again.</i>

341
00:27:54.965 --> 00:27:56.091
[Jian] No umbrella?

342
00:27:58.010 --> 00:28:00.596
I forgot my umbrella all the time
when I was little.

343
00:28:05.392 --> 00:28:06.768
[chuckles softly]

344
00:28:07.978 --> 00:28:10.314
See this? Do you want one?

345
00:28:13.901 --> 00:28:14.943
Try them on.

346
00:28:20.198 --> 00:28:23.368
It's all right. You can trust me.

347
00:28:24.536 --> 00:28:25.996
I'm friends with your father.

348
00:28:28.498 --> 00:28:29.583
[chuckles softly]

349
00:28:30.042 --> 00:28:31.209
[Jian] What?

350
00:28:31.293 --> 00:28:33.295
-[Jian] Oh. no.
-[child] Why are you so bad at this?

351
00:28:34.087 --> 00:28:36.256
[Jian] Why are you so good at this?

352
00:28:36.340 --> 00:28:37.466
-You--
-[child] Shoot!

353
00:28:37.674 --> 00:28:38.884
[car horn honking]

354
00:28:39.551 --> 00:28:41.470
Oh. hey. It's my dad.

355
00:28:56.026 --> 00:28:58.528
-General Suho!
-Hi. Dad!

356
00:29:00.614 --> 00:29:02.157
Where did you get this raincoat?

357
00:29:03.659 --> 00:29:06.620
Your friend. She gave me an extra one.

358
00:29:07.079 --> 00:29:08.956
Hm? My friend?

359
00:29:14.419 --> 00:29:17.089
Mr. Lee Jaeyoon. It's good to see you.

360
00:29:19.049 --> 00:29:20.550
Oh. it's been a while.

361
00:29:20.634 --> 00:29:22.427
Good to see you too. Hey.

362
00:29:23.428 --> 00:29:25.263
Suho. jump in the car. wait for Dad.

363
00:29:26.264 --> 00:29:28.725
[Suho] Thank you for the raincoat.
See you later.

364
00:29:28.809 --> 00:29:29.810
[Jian] Bye.

365
00:29:31.979 --> 00:29:34.898
[thunder rumbling]

366
00:29:43.115 --> 00:29:45.409
[Jian groans]

367
00:29:45.492 --> 00:29:47.744
[â™ª suspenseful music playing]

368
00:29:48.996 --> 00:29:51.415
What do you want? Why are you here?

369
00:29:51.498 --> 00:29:54.376
-[strained] Jeong Jian.
-Speak louder.

370
00:29:55.377 --> 00:29:58.630
[strained]
I'm Jeong Jian. Jeong Jinman's niece.

371
00:29:58.714 --> 00:30:01.508
Jeong Jian? Code Green?

372
00:30:03.885 --> 00:30:06.013
[Jian grunts. coughs]

373
00:30:06.763 --> 00:30:08.306
Did Jinman send you?

374
00:30:08.390 --> 00:30:12.352
That guy's a total scumbag.
He sent you after my son?

375
00:30:13.145 --> 00:30:15.689
It's pretty funny hearing
the word scumbagâ€¦

376
00:30:17.065 --> 00:30:19.067
-come out of your mouth.
-What?

377
00:30:19.818 --> 00:30:20.819
[sighs]

378
00:30:23.613 --> 00:30:26.825
The day Mr. Kim betrayed us
and brought all the Code Reds to attack.

379
00:30:27.784 --> 00:30:29.161
Why weren't you there?

380
00:30:29.244 --> 00:30:30.495
[scoffs]

381
00:30:31.329 --> 00:30:33.123
Did Jinman send you
to confront me about this?

382
00:30:34.207 --> 00:30:35.208
No.

383
00:30:36.168 --> 00:30:39.087
I didn't come here
to argue with you. all right?

384
00:30:39.921 --> 00:30:41.339
I'm here for a reason.

385
00:30:41.423 --> 00:30:45.260
Only two people on this Earth can persuade
the Code Reds to move.

386
00:30:45.343 --> 00:30:48.096
My uncle said one of them was Mr. Kim.
but he's dead.

387
00:30:49.514 --> 00:30:50.724
That's why I'm here.

388
00:30:51.516 --> 00:30:53.977
The only other person is you.
Mr. Ahn Seongbeom.

389
00:30:55.270 --> 00:30:58.774
-Will you please persuade the Code Reds?
-Maybe you haven't heard.

390
00:31:00.317 --> 00:31:01.485
[Seongbeom] I'm retired.

391
00:31:02.903 --> 00:31:03.945
[Jian] Wait.

392
00:31:05.572 --> 00:31:07.074
Aren't you even curious?

393
00:31:09.743 --> 00:31:11.203
I found your son.

394
00:31:12.079 --> 00:31:13.747
I knew who you wereâ€¦

395
00:31:14.664 --> 00:31:16.374
and what your alias was.

396
00:31:19.044 --> 00:31:20.378
You know what's cool?

397
00:31:21.213 --> 00:31:25.342
I offered the Code Purples extra money
to give me info on you. but they declined.

398
00:31:25.425 --> 00:31:28.929
They said it's an unwritten rule.
Never touch family.

399
00:31:30.222 --> 00:31:32.974
Every one of them refused to say anything.

400
00:31:33.725 --> 00:31:37.187
So how do you think it is
that I found out who you wereâ€¦

401
00:31:37.979 --> 00:31:40.190
and exactly where your son was?

402
00:31:48.406 --> 00:31:51.993
Babylon's been collecting
personal information on every Code Red.

403
00:31:52.077 --> 00:31:55.122
Those assholes put every single one
of you under surveillance.

404
00:31:56.081 --> 00:31:57.124
[angrily] Why?

405
00:32:03.547 --> 00:32:04.714
Tell me why!

406
00:32:05.173 --> 00:32:07.801
I'm retired!
Why is Babylon digging up my information?

407
00:32:07.884 --> 00:32:09.469
Why do you think. huh?

408
00:32:10.345 --> 00:32:11.638
It's always about money.

409
00:32:11.721 --> 00:32:13.765
Babylon is a big corporation

410
00:32:13.849 --> 00:32:15.976
and they're trying to swallow murthehelp.
to take over.

411
00:32:16.852 --> 00:32:18.311
I'll be blunt with you.

412
00:32:19.104 --> 00:32:22.649
The Babylon division from Japan
came to take murthehelp from us.

413
00:32:23.567 --> 00:32:25.694
They've been trying to mobilize Code Reds.

414
00:32:26.319 --> 00:32:29.865
They've even created a fake app
and are recruiting people without codes.

415
00:32:32.159 --> 00:32:33.994
They'll probably start a war with us.

416
00:32:34.953 --> 00:32:36.621
We don't have enough manpower.

417
00:32:37.747 --> 00:32:38.790
We need your help.

418
00:32:44.629 --> 00:32:46.423
Jeong Jinman. you listening?

419
00:32:46.506 --> 00:32:47.841
<i>Your niece has guts.</i>

420
00:32:48.508 --> 00:32:51.469
<i>But if you ever try to send anyone</i>
<i>to my son again.</i>

421
00:32:51.553 --> 00:32:52.804
<i>I promise you.</i>

422
00:32:52.888 --> 00:32:56.766
<i>I'll have no problems tearing apart</i>
<i>and killing both you and your niece.</i>

423
00:32:56.850 --> 00:33:00.353
<i>The only reason I'm holding back now</i>
<i>is as a final courtesy to you</i>

424
00:33:00.437 --> 00:33:02.189
<i>as an old colleague of mine.</i>

425
00:33:03.982 --> 00:33:07.319
[â™ª tense pensive music playing]

426
00:33:15.285 --> 00:33:16.411
[Jian sighs]

427
00:33:16.786 --> 00:33:18.455
[Jian] I think I messed it up.

428
00:33:19.873 --> 00:33:21.249
Please come and get me.

429
00:33:37.349 --> 00:33:40.685
You won't be able to change
Ahn Seongbeom's mind that easily.

430
00:33:40.769 --> 00:33:41.770
Don't give up yet.

431
00:33:43.313 --> 00:33:45.815
I didn't go to see his son
to threaten his family.

432
00:33:47.234 --> 00:33:48.693
[sighs]

433
00:33:50.195 --> 00:33:51.780
It just backfired.

434
00:33:52.781 --> 00:33:53.949
Jianâ€¦

435
00:33:55.492 --> 00:33:57.369
you probably feel that

436
00:33:57.452 --> 00:34:00.956
your uncle really messed up your life
by involving you in all of this.

437
00:34:01.039 --> 00:34:02.707
But he really does care.

438
00:34:02.791 --> 00:34:05.835
And trust me. he understands
the pain of losing someone you love.

439
00:34:07.420 --> 00:34:10.632
Jinman's lost a lot of people
in every stage of his life.

440
00:34:10.715 --> 00:34:14.761
As a soldier. a mercenary.
and long after leaving Babylon.

441
00:34:16.596 --> 00:34:17.722
It's been hard.

442
00:34:19.224 --> 00:34:21.685
Jinman's experienced so much loss thatâ€¦

443
00:34:22.394 --> 00:34:25.855
at some point he just accepted
this endless cycle of pain.

444
00:34:25.939 --> 00:34:28.608
That's why he's so guarded with everyone.

445
00:34:31.236 --> 00:34:33.989
Your uncle wanted you
to be strong and resilient.

446
00:34:34.739 --> 00:34:37.492
He just doesn't want you
to end up like he did.

447
00:34:38.535 --> 00:34:40.745
I don't want to end up like him either.

448
00:34:45.375 --> 00:34:47.502
I'm not going to do things like he did.

449
00:34:49.129 --> 00:34:50.130
Ever.

450
00:35:11.693 --> 00:35:13.486
I heard that you want to spar with me.

451
00:35:13.570 --> 00:35:15.238
Since Master Pasin's not here--

452
00:35:15.947 --> 00:35:17.324
[groans]

453
00:35:22.203 --> 00:35:24.581
[â™ª upbeat music playing]

454
00:35:30.337 --> 00:35:33.840
Inventory check is the basics
of running the shopping mall.

455
00:35:34.924 --> 00:35:38.053
Finish all of this today
and make sure you get it inspected.

456
00:35:40.639 --> 00:35:42.182
[Minhye grunts]

457
00:35:42.265 --> 00:35:43.850
[Jian grunts]

458
00:35:43.933 --> 00:35:45.352
[Jinwoo] This is 9 mm.

459
00:35:45.435 --> 00:35:47.312
This is 5.56.

460
00:35:47.395 --> 00:35:49.481
and this is 7.62.

461
00:35:49.564 --> 00:35:53.777
Simply put. the larger the caliber.
the more damage it does.

462
00:35:53.902 --> 00:35:56.488
[gunshots]

463
00:35:57.781 --> 00:35:59.824
[Minhye] A longer barrel
increases the range.

464
00:36:00.533 --> 00:36:03.495
When the sun's in front of you.
close the scope cover

465
00:36:04.371 --> 00:36:05.455
and look in the middle.

466
00:36:06.414 --> 00:36:08.958
Or you'll give yourself away
because of the sun's reflection.

467
00:36:10.168 --> 00:36:12.212
You can ask Brother
to give you a few of these.

468
00:36:17.550 --> 00:36:18.968
[gunshot]

469
00:36:19.344 --> 00:36:21.429
In order to prepare for hacker attacks.

470
00:36:21.513 --> 00:36:25.809
we maintain our security by switching
the site cover every 72 hours.

471
00:36:32.816 --> 00:36:34.984
Click the invisible button
under the event tag

472
00:36:35.068 --> 00:36:37.153
and it'll reveal the login
to the real site.

473
00:36:37.237 --> 00:36:39.531
When you log in
using the three biometric credentials

474
00:36:39.614 --> 00:36:42.992
that you originally registered with.
along with the code.

475
00:36:44.119 --> 00:36:46.705
you will get access
to the real murthehelp.

476
00:36:47.664 --> 00:36:50.041
What'd you do? Why'd you get denied?

477
00:36:50.667 --> 00:36:52.043
Poor circulation.

478
00:37:01.803 --> 00:37:04.055
[â™ª upbeat music continues]

479
00:37:04.556 --> 00:37:07.392
[Jian and Minhye grunting]

480
00:37:16.568 --> 00:37:17.861
No!

481
00:37:20.071 --> 00:37:22.532
[panting]

482
00:37:25.618 --> 00:37:27.328
You already finished dismantling it?

483
00:37:29.831 --> 00:37:32.917
This clover protected my life
when I escaped North Korea.

484
00:37:33.001 --> 00:37:34.461
It's yours now.

485
00:37:34.544 --> 00:37:35.879
You're giving it to me?

486
00:37:35.962 --> 00:37:39.340
My wishes all came true already.
I don't need it anymore.

487
00:37:43.678 --> 00:37:45.764
[Jian] Thank you. as always. Director Kim.

488
00:37:46.681 --> 00:37:51.186
Let's begin the new company agreement
between Jaewon Co. Ltd. and murthehelp.

489
00:37:52.896 --> 00:37:55.648
[gunfire]

490
00:38:11.539 --> 00:38:12.540
[gunfire]

491
00:38:12.624 --> 00:38:13.917
-[â™ª music ends]
-This way. hurry.

492
00:38:18.505 --> 00:38:19.547
[shushes]

493
00:38:21.549 --> 00:38:25.720
This place is a place only the boss
and I know about.

494
00:38:41.486 --> 00:38:44.489
Jeong Jian. listen well.

495
00:38:45.824 --> 00:38:51.079
